=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1471193-callings-question?p=1471229#post1471229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315311/Mysteries-of-the-World-The-Scion-Second-Edition-Companion\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Scion 2E Companion: Mysteries of the World</b></a> - are rules how to build alternative Callings etc. But, in reality, they are just much more focused Callings. If normal <i>Beasts</i> let you talk and change with all animals - Calling <i>Beasts ( Squirels)</i> let you talk and change only Squirels.<br /> <br /> ( But <b>Mysteries of the World</b> is great read, and I advice to look on it for each Story Guide before they run game in <b>Scion</b>! Gooooo <i>Myth Levels</i> and <i>Pantheon of Atlantis</i>!)</div> </div> </div> </div>the rules you are talking are not about Callings, but purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar